(4) NON-CIRCULARITY: bounds NOT using M(S)>=1/N
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  (B1)  dip <= 1/lcm(q,n) ?   (purely arithmetic in q,n)
     violations of dip<=1/lcm: 4
     tightest dip/(1/lcm): 1.0606 at n=7 q=4 k=1 dip=5/132 1/lcm=1/28

  (B4)  flank <= n  for binding pair (flank,w)?
     violations of flank<=n: 0
     max flank: 13 at n=14 q=2 k=5

  (CRUX) binding D=flank+w, M(S)=j/D.  D<=N*j  <=>  M(S)>=1/N (tautology).
         INDEPENDENT route would be: j (crossing index) bounded below by
         (flank,w) arithmetic so that j/D >= 1/N follows WITHOUT assuming it.

